CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98 --unwind 4
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constructed once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ state kept between calls: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ copy-initialized once: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [stmt.dcl]/3: the dynamic initialization of a block-scope static
variable happens the first time control passes through its declaration.
The front end ran the constructor at every pass (a documented
approximation), so instance() reset its counter on each call (bin53).
The initialization is now guarded by a static flag set when it completes
(an initialization exited by an exception is tried again, as /3
requires).  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
